which re-inserts the comma when rendering the number back to the DOM.</p>

<h4>Sort by Another Value</h4>

<p>Sometimes, we need one column to sort based on some other attribute.
For example, maybe we have a column which needs to sort on another
hidden column. We can use the <code>data-dynatable-sorts</code> attribute o=
n the
column header to let dynatable know.</p>

<div class=3D"highlight"><pre><code class=3D"html"><span class=3D"nt">&lt;t=
able</span> <span class=3D"na">id=3D</span><span class=3D"s">"sorting-examp=
le"</span><span class=3D"nt">&gt;</span>
  <span class=3D"nt">&lt;thead&gt;</span>
    <span class=3D"nt">&lt;tr&gt;</span>
      <span class=3D"nt">&lt;th&gt;</span>Name<span class=3D"nt">&lt;/th&gt=
;</span>
      <span class=3D"nt">&lt;th</span> <span class=3D"na">data-dynatable-so=
rts=3D</span><span class=3D"s">"computerYear"</span><span class=3D"nt">&gt;=
</span>Year<span class=3D"nt">&lt;/th&gt;</span>
      <span class=3D"nt">&lt;th</span> <span class=3D"na">style=3D</span><s=
pan class=3D"s">"display: none"</span><span class=3D"nt">&gt;</span>Compute=
r Year<span class=3D"nt">&lt;/th&gt;</span>
    <span class=3D"nt">&lt;/tr&gt;</span>
  <span class=3D"nt">&lt;/thead&gt;</span>
  <span class=3D"nt">&lt;tbody&gt;</span>
    <span class=3D"nt">&lt;tr&gt;</span>
      <span class=3D"nt">&lt;td&gt;</span>Steve<span class=3D"nt">&lt;/td&g=
t;</span>
      <span class=3D"nt">&lt;td&gt;</span>Two Thousand and Thirteen<span cl=
ass=3D"nt">&lt;/td&gt;</span>
      <span class=3D"nt">&lt;td&gt;</span>2013<span class=3D"nt">&lt;/td&gt=
;</span>
    <span class=3D"nt">&lt;/tr&gt;</span>
  <span class=3D"nt">&lt;/tbody&gt;</span>
<span class=3D"nt">&lt;/table&gt;</span>
</code></pre></div>


<p>In the above example, dynatable will detect that the last column heading
is hidden, and will hide all cells under that column, and it will sort
the "Year" column based on the attribute in the last column.</p>

<p>If we have a column we don't want to be sortable, we just add the
<code>data-dynatable-no-sort</code> attribute.</p>

